Unpeel: smaller standard pages for the Host-side VT.

Why: the private "pty-core" design record, 'Round 3, Lane 3'. Upstream's
standard page is ~400 KiB and PageList.minMaxSize forces at least two
pages, so any scrollback byte budget under ~1 MiB is silently raised to
that floor (a filled 80x24 Host terminal measured 778 KiB instead of
286 KiB on ghostty 6ba144158). Applied only when building the vendored
libghostty-vt.a for unpeel-host (build.sh); the app's GhosttyKit build is
untouched.

diff --git a/src/terminal/page.zig b/src/terminal/page.zig
index 48d405b5f..ba421c6b2 100644
--- a/src/terminal/page.zig
+++ b/src/terminal/page.zig
@@ -1887,11 +1887,18 @@ pub const Page = struct {
 /// The standard capacity is chosen as the fast-path for allocation since
 /// pages of standard capacity use a pooled allocator instead of single-use
 /// mmaps.
+///
+/// Unpeel: a much smaller standard page than upstream's, so
+/// PageList.minMaxSize (two pages) stays inside the Host's 256 KiB
+/// scrollback budget and a filled 80x24 terminal stays under 400 KiB
+/// resident. Styles and grapheme bytes are sized for a terminal that is
+/// read by a Host, not rendered; pages that need more grow to non-standard
+/// capacity exactly as upstream does.
 pub const std_capacity: Capacity = .{
     .cols = 215,
-    .rows = 215,
+    .rows = 32,
     .styles = 128,
-    .grapheme_bytes = if (builtin.is_test) 512 else 8192,
+    .grapheme_bytes = if (builtin.is_test) 512 else 2048,
 };
 
 /// The size of this page.
